  <div class="slide caption-page" data-document-role="page" data-label="C16 - Caption (copy/paste)">
    <div class="caption-flag">Caption - not for posting</div>
    <div class="caption-body">Letting your sensitive child wear noise-cancelling headphones in a loud place is not avoidance. It is giving their brain a break.<br><br>Research finds that reducing sound input can lower the physical stress response a noisy environment creates. For a sensitive nervous system that is already working overtime to filter input, that means more brain capacity freed up for everything else, focusing, connecting, staying regulated.<br><br>We would never call glasses a crutch for someone who needs them. Supporting the senses works the same way. A tool that helps a child's brain stay out of overload is not letting them off the hook. It is helping them cope with a world that lands harder for them. A tool is not a crutch.</div>
    <div class="caption-tags">#noisecancellingheadphones #sensorytools #stressresponse</div>
    <div class="caption-accounts">Tag: none needed</div>
  </div>


