  <div class="slide caption-page" data-document-role="page" data-label="C18 - Caption (copy/paste)">
    <div class="caption-flag">Caption - not for posting</div>
    <div class="caption-body">A simple warning before a transition works for a real, brain-based reason: it gives the brain time to shift gears.<br><br>Switching from one activity to another draws on brain systems that are still maturing in young children. Sudden change asks those systems to change direction with no runway, and that abruptness is its own kind of overload. A clear heads-up gives the brain a moment to prepare instead of being caught completely off guard.<br><br>Research even shows that cues signaling an upcoming switch improve how well kids manage the change. So 'five more minutes, then we clean up' is not just being polite. It is scaffolding a real brain process. You are lending time to a system that genuinely needs a runway. A little warning turns out to be a big kindness.</div>
    <div class="caption-tags">#transitionwarning #transitions #setshifting</div>
    <div class="caption-accounts">Tag: none needed</div>
