  <div class="slide caption-page" data-document-role="page" data-label="C19 - Caption (copy/paste)">
    <div class="caption-flag">Caption - not for posting</div>
    <div class="caption-body">Two children can stand in the exact same room and have two very different brains taking it all in.<br><br>How much sensory input a brain registers and reacts to varies a great deal from one child to the next, and that variation has a biological basis. So the birthday party that lights one child up can genuinely flood their sibling. Same music, same crowd, two completely different nervous systems processing it.<br><br>Neither brain is doing it wrong. They are simply tuned to different volumes. When we compare them, whether one child is being too sensitive or the other too wild, we miss that they were never really in the same environment at all. Same room is not the same experience.</div>
