    <div class="caption-body">Your sensitive child is not trying to embarrass you in the grocery store. Their brain is caught in a genuine sensory storm.<br><br>Fluorescent lights, the freezer hum, overhead announcements, crowds, and a dozen competing smells all hit the brain at the same time. For a sensitive nervous system that does less automatic filtering, processing all of that at once is an overwhelming amount of work while also trying to hold it together.<br><br>So the meltdown by the checkout is not a performance staged for you. It is a brain that finally ran out of room to cope with everything coming in. The store is genuinely a lot, especially for a small brain still learning to handle all of it at once. The store is a lot, even for a small brain.</div>
